            </div> 
                <p class="snippet" >
                    Distinguished: <b>Andrews v. Grand &amp; Toy Alberta</b> Ltd., [1978] 2 S.C.R. 229; Thornton v. School District No. 57 (Prince George), [1978] 2 S.C.R. 267; Arnold v. Teno, [1978] 2 S.C.R. 287; referred to: Massie &amp; Renwick Ltd. v. Underwriters’ Survey Bureau Ltd., [1940] S.C.R. 218; Théberge v. Galerie d’Art du Petit &nbsp;&nbsp;[...]&nbsp;&nbsp;[15] The Court of Appeal held that the cap established in the Andrews trilogy (<b>Andrews v. Grand &amp; Toy Alberta</b> Ltd., [1978] 2 S.C.R. 229, Thornton v. School District No. 57 (Prince George), [1978] 2 S.C.R. 267, and Arnold v. Teno, [1978] 2 S.C.R. 287) was applicable to the award for psychological suffering and reduced 
                </p>
